virglrenderer: core profile shaders ask for GLSL 3.30, no extensions that are core

What: on a desktop core profile that supports GLSL 3.30 (macOS: 4.10), every
translated shader is "#version 330" or newer instead of 140/150. Every
desktop "#extension" line goes through one table of the GLSL version where
the extension is core (ext_core_glsl_ver), compared with the "#version" that
emit_header() really writes (desktop_glsl_ver(): compute shaders stay 330);
the separate version checks next to some lines are gone. Not in the table:
extensions without a core version and those whose GLSL the translator writes
with the extension's names (textureQueryLOD, *ARB functions).
Why: Apple's core profile refuses floatBitsToInt()/intBitsToFloat() and friends
below 3.30, and many translations use them without setting SHADER_REQ_INTS (e.g.
integer vertex attributes passed on: dEQP-GLES3.functional.shaders.precision.int.*).
It also refuses "#extension" lines for what it has in core, e.g.
GL_ARB_draw_instanced (Chrome's instanced WebGL shaders). One refused shader
stopped the guest's whole GL context, so every later draw of that app was
black (dEQP-GLES3 in one process: 455/896 pass).
Upstreamable (desktop core profiles only; GLES and compatibility hosts are
unchanged); not sent.
Overlap: gpu-robust's virgl-core-instance-id.patch does the ARB_draw_instanced
part only and touches the same loop; both apply in either order (checked),
drop virgl-core-instance-id.patch when both land.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c (generated GLSL compiled by the
Mac's OpenGL; every case checks the version and extension lines; a compute
shader that needs 4.30 keeps its extension lines; fails without this patch).
